# Do not explain the site to itself

Published copy (`*.html`, speech JSON, widget intro text, news notes) is for residents. A sentence that only tells the reader where this website keeps something, how a page is wired, or how the editor scored a row is slop. Delete it in the same edit. Do not replace it with a softer version of the same lecture.

Parent: `no-ai-slop-on-site.mdc`.

## Ban

| Slop | Write instead |
|---|---|
| “Crossville-specific contacts and templates stay on this site.” | The contacts, or a plain link. Then stop. |
| “Crossville records stay on this site.” / “Meeting times and speeches stay on this page.” | Omit. |
| “Crossville-specific Tennessee cases and local action tools remain on the home page.” | Link the home page if a reader needs it. Do not narrate the filing. |
| “The East Tennessee investigation this site is patterned after…” | What that neighbor site is. |
| “We still link primary sources for Crossville-specific claims.” | Omit. |
| “These counts come from the case tables on this site. Geography hubs:” | The place links, with no label about hubs or tables. |
| “Same searchable tables as the National page, Tennessee only.” | “Tennessee rows.” plus the National link if needed. |
| “…are in the JSON catalog, not repeated here.” | The fact, or “Pauses are in the cancellation table.” |
| “Extra rules without cancel are not scored as cancel.” / “not scored as a yes or no in the table” | The public fact. “That is not a promise to cancel.” |
| “This site does not name civilian speakers.” | Omit the name. Do not announce the omission. |
| “Newcomers without a published email are omitted.” | Name who the button emails. |
| “Treat that as Inquest’s summary of the same rivalry already on this page.” | Inquest’s facts. Stop. |
| “The signed agreement is now on this site.” | “The signed agreement is posted.” |

Also ban: “patterned after,” “stay on this site,” “stay on this page,” “remain on the home page,” “not repeated here,” “cross-links,” “geography hubs,” “Case catalogs (on this site).”

## Still fine

A link a resident can use. A status fact (cameras stay, council has not voted). A footnote Case_ID. “Not an endorsement.” “Not legal advice.”

## Check

Read every new sentence as a stranger. If it would only make sense to the person who built the page, strip it before finishing.
